# Toolchain versions for asdf / mise / rtx.
#
# This is a pin REGISTRY, not an install manifest. `asdf install` here
# materialises exactly ONE toolchain — Node — because that is the only one in
# this list with no manager of its own: the Flutter SDK comes from flutter.dev,
# Rust from rustup, Go from the distro, Terraform from tfenv, Deno from its own
# installer, and having asdf put a second copy of any of them on the machine is
# not what anyone wants. The other six lines are therefore COMMENTED on purpose
# (decisions § 1536); what a contributor installs from is the Prerequisites
# table in docs/architecture/monorepo.md, which is read against these same pins.
#
# The format is `<plugin> <version>` per line. Every version here is CHECKED
# against the pin the repo itself enforces, by scripts/check_toolchain_pins.mjs
# — including the commented lines, because a commented pin is a claim the next
# reader will uncomment (decisions § 911). The sources of truth are:
#
#   nodejs    — every workflow's `actions/setup-node` step (exact, not a major:
#               CI names the patch since decisions § 1214, so a bare major here
#               would be a pin nothing compares — § 1216)
#   rust      — apps/custom_watch/rust-toolchain.toml
#   golang    — apps/*/go.mod
#   flutter   — each workflow's top-level env.FLUTTER_VERSION
#   terraform — .github/workflows/terraform.yml
#   deno      — each workflow's `denoland/setup-deno` step (exact, not a
#               channel: a Deno minor carries new `deno check` diagnostics)
#
# The rest carry no in-repo pin, so nothing can check them: python3 / zola are
# whatever the runner ships.

